From: LuneOS <team@webos-ports.org>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] gstreamer: report the camera position from the libcamera
 device properties

QGstreamerVideoDevices::findVideoInputs() fills in the description, the id and
the isDefault flag of every camera it finds, but never touches
QCameraDevicePrivate::position. Every camera therefore reports
QCameraDevice::UnspecifiedPosition, and an application has no way to tell a
front camera from a back one.

libcamera does publish this. Its GStreamer element exposes the camera's
Location property on the GstDevice:

    camera-properties, api.libcamera.Location=(string)CameraLocationFront, ...
    camera-properties, api.libcamera.Location=(string)CameraLocationBack, ...

Map it onto QCameraDevice::Position. On a PinePhone Pro this makes the ov8858
report FrontFace and the imx258 BackFace instead of both reporting
UnspecifiedPosition, so a camera application's front/back switch can work.

Devices that do not carry the property, including v4l2 ones, are unaffected and
keep reporting UnspecifiedPosition.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
diff -ruN vd_a/src/plugins/multimedia/gstreamer/qgstreamervideodevices.cpp vd_b/src/plugins/multimedia/gstreamer/qgstreamervideodevices.cpp
--- a/src/plugins/multimedia/gstreamer/qgstreamervideodevices.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/multimedia/gstreamer/qgstreamervideodevices.cpp
@@ -82,6 +82,18 @@
             QGstStructureView view{ properties };
             auto def = view["is-default"].toBool();
             info->isDefault = def && *def;
+
+            /*
+             * libcamera publishes which way a camera faces as a device
+             * property. Without it every camera reports UnspecifiedPosition and
+             * an application cannot tell the front camera from the back one.
+             */
+            if (const char *location = view["api.libcamera.Location"].toString()) {
+                if (!qstrcmp(location, "CameraLocationFront"))
+                    info->position = QCameraDevice::FrontFace;
+                else if (!qstrcmp(location, "CameraLocationBack"))
+                    info->position = QCameraDevice::BackFace;
+            }
         }
 
         if (info->isDefault)
